{#
  Session turn user message, v6 (design s05-acb D4). Language-neutral wrapper (only tags
  and values), identical to v5 except for the optional `<critic_feedback>` block. The
  attachments go before the transcript (long documents first, the request last), each
  after the `--- attachment: <name> ---` separator with its masked text, or `[…]` in the
  copy stored in the history (`text` is none). The transcript goes verbatim and
  unescaped. Only on a retry of the Actor-Critic-Boss review, the `critical`/`major`
  issues of the last Critic review (filtered in code) go last, after the transcript:
  the most recent instruction. The fixed text is English, like the other instructions;
  the descriptions are printed verbatim, in the session language. Never in the copy
  stored in the history. Without feedback this template renders exactly as v5's.
#}
<project_type>{{ project_type }}</project_type>
{% if attachments %}
<attachments>
{% for attachment in attachments %}
--- attachment: {{ attachment.name }} ---
{{ attachment.text if attachment.text is not none else attachment_placeholder }}
{% endfor %}
</attachments>
{% endif %}
<transcript>
{{ transcript }}
</transcript>
{% if critic_feedback %}
<critic_feedback>
A previous draft of this estimate was reviewed by an independent auditor. Produce a new estimate that fixes these issues and keeps everything else consistent:
{% for issue in critic_issues %}
- [{{ issue.severity }}] {{ issue.category }} at {{ issue.field_path }}: {{ issue.description }}{{ " (suggested fix: " ~ issue.suggested_fix ~ ")" if issue.suggested_fix else "" }}
{% endfor %}
</critic_feedback>
{% endif %}
